{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/ConsentDropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait until they are read. A record dropped for room is reported as it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped; while that report waits unread, later ones merge into it, one report counting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them all across their timestamps. So the reports waiting unread hold at most one overflow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report between any two others (denials and finished trackers), however many events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overflow. The sequence has one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consumer, and ends once the consent is gone."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8Trackers7ConsentV11dropReportsScSyA